Emerald 3DS changes to pret/pokeemerald 76463dac15cad36aca5e2b3f6366abf9e53f814f: Japanese texts whose values the code places
Applies after 0073-japanese-title-version-palette.patch; apply with tools/bootstrap.py.

Of the Japanese texts whose placeholders differ from the international ones, three
need code (the others are filled by code both games run, see docs/JAPANESE.md):
the Exp. Points message has no third battle buffer in the Japanese ROM, which puts
"gained" after the name in the first and the number in the second; the trainer
card's back appends gText_Var1sTrainerCard to the name and prints the link battle
wins and losses apart from gText_WinsLosses, with that ROM's stat positions and
small font. Other languages are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/battle_script_commands.c b/src/battle_script_commands.c
index 4ae4c71..c68baec 100644
--- a/src/battle_script_commands.c
+++ b/src/battle_script_commands.c
@@ -3490,10 +3490,25 @@ static void Cmd_getexp(void)
                     else
 #endif
                     {
+#if GAME_LANGUAGE == LANGUAGE_JAPANESE
+                    // The Japanese text is "{B_BUFF1}{B_BUFF2} Exp. Points": that
+                    // ROM has no third buffer and puts 'gained' (or 'gained a
+                    // boosted') after the name in the first, the number in the second.
+                    gBattleTextBuff1[0] = B_BUFF_PLACEHOLDER_BEGIN;
+                    gBattleTextBuff1[1] = B_BUFF_MON_NICK_WITH_PREFIX;
+                    gBattleTextBuff1[2] = gBattleStruct->expGetterBattlerId;
+                    gBattleTextBuff1[3] = gBattleStruct->expGetterMonId;
+                    gBattleTextBuff1[4] = B_BUFF_STRING;
+                    gBattleTextBuff1[5] = i;
+                    gBattleTextBuff1[6] = (i & 0xFF00) >> 8;
+                    gBattleTextBuff1[7] = B_BUFF_EOS;
+                    PREPARE_WORD_NUMBER_BUFFER(gBattleTextBuff2, 5, gBattleMoveDamage);
+#else
                     PREPARE_MON_NICK_WITH_PREFIX_BUFFER(gBattleTextBuff1, gBattleStruct->expGetterBattlerId, gBattleStruct->expGetterMonId);
                     // buffer 'gained' or 'gained a boosted'
                     PREPARE_STRING_BUFFER(gBattleTextBuff2, i);
                     PREPARE_WORD_NUMBER_BUFFER(gBattleTextBuff3, 5, gBattleMoveDamage);
+#endif
 
                     PrepareStringBattle(STRINGID_PKMNGAINEDEXP, gBattleStruct->expGetterBattlerId);
                     }
